re really flexible and they're  really cheap and then i got five of  these clamps that you can find at any  hardware store  i got the two inch sizes to make sure  that they fit on the handles above the  doors i'm gonna use the front right  handle the back right handle  the back left handle and there's none on  the left in the front so  i'm gonna use the visor i'm gonna push  the front seats forward so i can clamp  the two mats overhead  i'll clamp them together in the back and  because the mats are meant to prevent  punctures  i can actually remove one of the  headrests and use that to squeeze the  mat at the very top of the back window  now i'll fold the mats into the edges  and corners and then push the two front  seats back  and these will act as a reflection  filter on both sides of the mic if you  want to go really hard you could bring  in some  acoustic panels and just lean them  around the sides and then set up bass  traps on the floor but for most cases  it's not really necessary so we're gonna  test without it this is the recording  gear that i use at my desk  really just for yelling at teammates in  apex legends note the 15  desk arm this is important this is going  to let us stick the mic into the  recording booth but we do need a surface  to clamp it on  i forget what this thing is called but  we're gonna open it up and clamp the mic  onto the front wall  and here's what it looks like you see  the mic is between the two chairs and it  can be pulled back  into the booth hovering right at  recording level here's what it looks  like from the inside  and the mic is in a good spot so i'll  plug in the xlr cable  and then use that middle thing for cable  management the other end will go into  the audio interface  which will be connected to my laptop  which is also connected to the midi  keyboard on the dashboard  so now i guess we just hop into the  producer's chair and start cooking  something up  i found a copyright-free song i can just  cover but i can only use stock logic  plugins  so let's see what we can do  all right so we got a rough instrumental  so i'll hop into the back in the  recording booth where i'll track all the  vocals  and do the mixing mastering arrangement  and all that other stuff  and there we go um it turns out  acoustics won't fix your technique but  we got something  and if it's not studio quality i won't  be too mad because it is a car but let's  see how close we got  the dawn's early light  was so proudly we failed  at the twilight's last gleaming  whose bright stripes and bright stars  through the perilous spike  all the ramparts we've washed were so  gallantly  [Music]  you get the point obviously the sound  quality is not professional  but for most people it's definitely good  enough and you can just focus on getting  better at your craft  until it makes more sense to upgrade to  a studio setup it will be better if you  have a car with nicer sound deadening  but other than that for how  straightforward this is i think it  worked out pretty well so thank you for  watching i hope you found this helpful  drop a like comment subscribe and i'll  see you later  [Music]  you
 

